// Prose that copy and paste must give back as it was written: long words
// that the narrow page hyphenates, ligatures, dashes, quotes, a footnote.
title "Paste Prose"
paper a5

The internationalization of incomprehensibility is uncharacteristically straightforward for electroencephalographers.
An efficient official finds the affluent office's scaffolding difficult and fluffy.
Pages 10--20 cover the "standard" case---the one everybody's textbook treats.
Counterrevolutionaries misunderstand photolithographic characterizations of thermodynamically irreversible transformations.^[A footnote, with notwithstanding hyphenation.]
Multidimensional decompositions of representation-theoretic constructions are indispensable.
